Neon is developed by chronicaly.
The motion blur renderer, render hooks, strength curve and shaders are adapted
from chronicaly's Unity client (https://github.com/chronicaly/unity), revision
4ba0d6e: MotionBlurModule.java, MotionBlurRenderer.java, MixinMotionBlur.java,
and assets/unity/shaders/core/motion_blur.{vsh,fsh}. These are Unity-owned
implementations, ported at the author's request. They contain no MotionBlur
Plus runtime code. Neon adds its own settings integration and resource cleanup.
Other Unity components were inspected as behavior and Minecraft 26.2 API
references. Unity's module infrastructure and third-party ports are not bundled.

Armor HUD's vanilla presentation and configuration were used as a design reference:
https://github.com/uku3lig/armor-hud (BerdinskiyBear and contributors / uku3lig).
No source code or assets were copied from that project. Slot frames are drawn
from Minecraft's own hotbar sprite, honoring the active resource pack.

The Gradle wrapper is Copyright the Gradle original authors and licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
Fabric API and Fabric Loader are external dependencies, not repackaged source.
Mod Menu is an optional integration, not bundled.

The Neon interface includes Inter by The Inter Project Authors, distributed
under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. The full license is bundled at
licenses/Inter-OFL.txt. Source: https://github.com/rsms/inter/releases/tag/v4.1
At the author's explicit request, the HUD editor now ports Unity's root/group/
boolean/range row construction from HudEditorScreen.java, diagonal corner resize
calculation from HudResize.java, and CompactMotion.java (revision 5bbd639).
These Unity-owned implementations are adapted to Neon's armor/totem config,
native-resolution font renderer, Fabric input, and undo history. Unity's separate
checkout and installed artifacts are preserved; no Unity UI assets are bundled.

The inline color picker ports the interaction and HSV/alpha model from Unity's
ColorPicker.java, ClientScreen.java, and ColorArgumentType.java at revision
5bbd639, with Neon's layout, native typography, GPU gradients, and undo adapters.

Neon's short module-enabling sound is original deterministic synthesis, generated by
tools/generate-ui-sounds.ps1 and encoded as Ogg Vorbis. No Minecraft samples or
third-party audio assets are included.
